{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat /Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/dryrun14/packet.json'","aggregated_output":"[\n {\n  \"question\": \"Will China authorize NVIDIA to sell H200 chips in mainland China by 2027-01-31, as verified by an official Chinese government or regulatory announcement or licensing decision, or by NVIDIA disclosing that H200 sales or shipments to China have resumed?\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2027-01-31\",\n  \"rungs\": [\n   \"rung 1 Yes: By 2027-01-31, China has authorized H200 sales in mainland China, or NVIDIA has disclosed that H200 sales or shipments to China have resumed.\",\n   \"rung 2 Ruled out: By 2027-01-31, China has formally denied authorization or officially decided to continue barring H200 imports. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-02 and stands on 2027-01-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n   \"rung 3 Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.\"\n  ],\n  \"facts_on_the_due_day\": [\n   {\n    \"scenario\": 1,\n    \"facts\": \"In March 2026 China officially decided to continue barring H200 imports. Nothing has been decided or announced since, and NVIDIA has disclosed no H200 sales or shipments to China.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"scenario\": 2,\n    \"facts\": \"In October 2026 China formally denied authorization for H200 sales. Nothing has changed since, and no sale has been disclosed.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"scenario\": 3,\n    \"facts\": \"In November 2026 China authorized H200 sales in mainland China.\"\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA’s Kyber NVL144 rack-scale system, paired with Rubin Ultra, make its first shipment by 2027-12-31, as verified by NVIDIA disclosure or an official shipment announcement?\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2027-12-31\",\n  \"rungs\": [\n   \"rung 1 Yes: NVIDIA’s Kyber NVL144 rack-scale system, paired with Rubin Ultra, makes its first shipment by 2027-12-31, verified by NVIDIA disclosure or an official shipment announcement.\",\n   \"rung 2 Ruled out: By 2027-12-31, NVIDIA has decided that Kyber NVL144 will not ship until 2028 or later, or has formally abandoned or cancelled the system. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole taken after 2026-07-05, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole after that day, stands on 2027-12-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n   \"rung 3 Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-12-31.\"\n  ],\n  \"facts_on_the_due_day\": [\n   {\n    \"scenario\": 4,\n    \"facts\": \"In November 2027 NVIDIA disclosed that the Kyber NVL144 rack-scale system, paired with Rubin Ultra, had made its first shipment.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"scenario\": 5,\n    \"facts\": \"In June 2026 NVIDIA decided that Kyber NVL144 would not ship until 2028. Nothing has changed since: NVIDIA has announced nothing new, and no shipment has been made.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"scenario\": 6,\n    \"facts\": \"In March 2027 NVIDIA announced that it had decided Kyber NVL144 will not ship until 2028. No shipment has been made.\"\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"question\": \"Will China permit NVIDIA to sell H200 AI chips in mainland China by January 31, 2027, as established by an official Chinese announcement or licensing decision, or by NVIDIA disclosing H200 sales or shipments to China?\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2027-01-31\",\n  \"rungs\": [\n   \"rung 1 Yes: By January 31, 2027, China has officially permitted H200 sales to mainland China, or NVIDIA has disclosed H200 sales or shipments to China.\",\n   \"rung 2 Ruled out: By January 31, 2027, a Chinese government or regulator has formally decided not to permit H200 sales, or formally decided to keep them barred, and that decision remains in force. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole taken after 2026-07-02, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole after that day, stands on 2027-01-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n   \"rung 3 Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.\"\n  ],\n  \"facts_on_the_due_day\": [\n   {\n    \"scenario\": 7,\n    \"facts\": \"In November 2026 China officially permitted H200 sales to mainland China.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"scenario\": 8,\n    \"facts\": \"In March 2026 Chinese regulators formally decided to keep H200 sales barred. That decision is still in force on the due day. Nothing has been decided or announced since, and no sale or shipment has been disclosed.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"scenario\": 9,\n    \"facts\": \"In October 2026 Chinese regulators formally decided not to permit H200 sales. That decision is in force on the due day. No sale or shipment has been disclosed.\"\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"question\": \"Will Chinese authorities approve imports of Nvidia H200 chips into China for Alibaba, ByteDance, DeepSeek, or other firms by January 31, 2027, as established by official Chinese government decisions or announcements?\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2027-01-31\",\n  \"rungs\": [\n   \"rung 1 Yes: Chinese authorities approve at least one of Alibaba, ByteDance, DeepSeek, or another Chinese firm to import Nvidia H200 chips by January 31, 2027, as shown by an official government decision or announcement.\",\n   \"rung 2 Ruled out: Chinese authorities formally decide not to approve H200 imports for any Chinese firms, or formally abandon or withdraw the plan to allow them, by January 31, 2027. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole taken after 2026-07-08, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole after that day, stands on 2027-01-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n   \"rung 3 Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.\"\n  ],\n  \"facts_on_the_due_day\": [\n   {\n    \"scenario\": 10,\n    \"facts\": \"In May 2026 Chinese authorities formally decided not to approve H200 imports for any Chinese firm. That decision is unchanged on the due day; nothing has been decided since, and no firm has been approved.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"scenario\": 11,\n    \"facts\": \"In October 2026 Chinese authorities approved Alibaba to import Nvidia H200 chips, as shown by an official announcement.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"scenario\": 12,\n    \"facts\": \"In November 2026 Chinese authorities formally decided not to approve H200 imports for any Chinese firm. No firm has been approved.\"\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"question\": \"Will the US Commerce Department or Bureau of Industry and Security impose a binding export-licensing rule or other formal escalated export restriction, beyond its May 2026 guidance, on AI-chip shipments to third countries such as Malaysia, Singapore, and Japan by Nvidia's FY2027 year-end, as established by a Federal Register rule, licence requirement, or formal export-control action?\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2027-01-31\",\n  \"rungs\": [\n   \"rung 1 Yes: By 2027-01-31, the US Commerce Department or Bureau of Industry and Security has issued or put into effect a binding export-licensing rule or other formal escalated export restriction, beyond its May 2026 guidance, on AI-chip shipments to third countries such as Malaysia, Singapore, or Japan.\",\n   \"rung 2 Ruled out: By 2027-01-31, the US Commerce Department or Bureau of Industry and Security has formally decided against, or formally abandoned or withdrawn, the proposed escalation to a binding export-licensing rule or other formal export restriction on AI-chip shipments to those third countries, and no such restriction has taken effect. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-14 and stands on 2027-01-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n   \"rung 3 Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.\"\n  ],\n  \"facts_on_the_due_day\": [\n   {\n    \"scenario\": 13,\n    \"facts\": \"In November 2026 the Commerce Department formally withdrew its proposed escalation to a binding export-licensing rule. No restriction beyond the May 2026 guidance has been issued or put into effect.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"scenario\": 14,\n    \"facts\": \"In October 2026 the Bureau of Industry and Security put into effect a binding export-licensing rule, beyond its May 2026 guidance, on AI-chip shipments to third countries.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"scenario\": 15,\n    \"facts\": \"In June 2026 the Commerce Department formally decided against a proposed escalation to a binding export-licensing rule. Nothing has been proposed or decided since, and no restriction beyond the May 2026 guidance has been issued or put into effect.\"\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"question\": \"Will China permit NVIDIA to sell H200 AI chips in mainland China by January 31, 2027, as established by an official Chinese announcement or licensing decision, or by NVIDIA disclosing H200 sales or shipments to China?\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2027-01-31\",\n  \"rungs\": [\n   \"rung 1 Yes: By January 31, 2027, China has officially permitted H200 sales to mainland China, or NVIDIA has disclosed H200 sales or shipments to China.\",\n   \"rung 2 Ruled out: By January 31, 2027, a Chinese government or regulator has formally decided not to permit H200 sales, or formally decided to keep them barred, and that decision remains in force. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-02 and stands on 2027-01-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n   \"rung 3 Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.\"\n  ],\n  \"facts_on_the_due_day\": [\n   {\n    \"scenario\": 16,\n    \"facts\": \"In October 2026 Chinese regulators formally decided not to permit H200 sales. That decision is in force on the due day. No sale or shipment has been disclosed.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"scenario\": 17,\n    \"facts\": \"In March 2026 Chinese regulators formally decided to keep H200 sales barred. That decision is still in force on the due day. Nothing has been decided or announced since, and no sale or shipment has been disclosed.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"scenario\": 18,\n    \"facts\": \"In November 2026 China officially permitted H200 sales to mainland China.\"\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA’s Kyber NVL144 rack-scale system, paired with Rubin Ultra, make its first shipment by 2027-12-31, as verified by NVIDIA disclosure or an official shipment announcement?\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2027-12-31\",\n  \"rungs\": [\n   \"rung 1 Yes: NVIDIA’s Kyber NVL144 rack-scale system, paired with Rubin Ultra, makes its first shipment by 2027-12-31, verified by NVIDIA disclosure or an official shipment announcement.\",\n   \"rung 2 Ruled out: By 2027-12-31, NVIDIA has decided that Kyber NVL144 will not ship until 2028 or later, or has formally abandoned or cancelled the system. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole, was made after 2026-07-05 and stands on 2027-12-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n   \"rung 3 Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-12-31.\"\n  ],\n  \"facts_on_the_due_day\": [\n   {\n    \"scenario\": 19,\n    \"facts\": \"In June 2026 NVIDIA decided that Kyber NVL144 would not ship until 2028. Nothing has changed since: NVIDIA has announced nothing new, and no shipment has been made.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"scenario\": 20,\n    \"facts\": \"In November 2027 NVIDIA disclosed that the Kyber NVL144 rack-scale system, paired with Rubin Ultra, had made its first shipment.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"scenario\": 21,\n    \"facts\": \"In March 2027 NVIDIA announced that it had decided Kyber NVL144 will not ship until 2028. No shipment has been mad